<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria has $234.7 mln Q1 C/A surplus.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria has $234.7 mln Q1 C/A surplus.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria posted a trade surplus of $234.7 million in the first quarter of this year after a surplus of $40.8 million end-1996 and a $175.3 million deficit a year ago, preliminary Bulgarian National Bank figures show.  </p>
<p>The first quarter surplus was attributed mainly to declining imports and a sharp depreciation of the national currency the lev, which boosted the competitiveness of Bulgarian production, the BNB said.</p>
<p> BULGARIA CURRENT ACCOUNT,   Q1'97	1996	  Q1'96</p>
<p>   million USD			+234.7     +40.8	 -175.3</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE		  +379.0    +208.0	  -32.8</p>
<p>   exports fob		 1,144.5   4,881.4	1,191.6</p>
<p>   imports fob		   765.5   4,673.4	1,224.4</p>
<p> SERVICES NET		    -25.8    +123.5	  -23.5</p>
<p> INCOME NET		     -153.7    -395.1	 -166.2</p>
<p>   receipts			 65.9     181.0	   54.6</p>
<p>   payments			219.6     576.1	  220.8</p>
<p> TRANSFERS NET		    35.2     104.4	   47.1</p>
<p>Trade figures based on customs data.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-981-4145</p>
